two years ago we hit rock bottom but  still we rise roses from the concrete we  blossom  I loved ones gone but never forgotten  the fight for justice continues in this  memorial service 72 seconds of silence  one for each victim of the Grenfell fire  two years have passed but the emotion is  still raw as names of those who died  were read aloud and remembered  Jeremiah Dean zeinab Dean vincent regina  fatima afro sahabi a [ __ ] a mayor  - chu ammidon bereaved relatives  survivors and community leaders came to  show respect and solidarity but it was  not only a day for remembrance there was  frustration - the lack of progress and  change Corinne mursili lost his uncle in  the fire and now campaigns with Grenfell  United we're demanding change so we want  the government to start listening to  things that they have heard before Brent  felt these are concerns that have been  made to the government before grandfa  even happened in terms of Building  Regulations you know government  ministers knew that there were issues  not only surrounding the cladding  dangerous materials that were being put  inside the buildings but also buildings  I didn't have sprinklers you know  buildings that the fire doors went fit  for purpose it just didn't work at all  this urgent call for action shared by  firefighters who've warned there could  be another catastrophic loss of life  unless more buildings are made safe  there are a lot of people still living  at risk in high-rise tower blocks over  300 tower blocks around the country  thousands and thousands of people living  at risk in these tower blocks the  government have made empty promises  nothing has happened the risk is still  there and that you would have expected a  government in this time in this day and  age to fulfill their promises and to  made safe dwellings for families in the  21st century like the 14th day of every  month since the grenfell fire a silent  walk  thousands marched through the streets  with bereaved relatives and survivors  joined by residents and political  figures including Labour's Jeremy Corbyn  this an opportunity to stand together  and unite this is not only about paying  tribute with 72 people who died this is  also about coming together and showing  strength demonstrating to the wider  public the people here are still  fighting and demanding change with  delays to the public inquiry and no  criminal charges for a few years at  least justice may be a way off with the  people of Grenfell are standing strong  they say they won't give up the fight  until people are safe in their homes so  a tragedy like grenfell can never happen  again  Charlotte Lomas Sky News
 

